    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0423" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2439c</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-07T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5236. Red Cross here is willing to undertake providing warm clothing, other than
                    uniforms, for 70,000 Czecho-Slovak troops in Siberia. Please ascertain,
                    discreetly, whether French Government contemplates any similar assistance which
                    would render it unnecessary for Red Cross to undertake full responsibility for
                    clothing, other than uniforms. Answer urgent.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d397-f1"
                    /></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
